{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And in craft.</b> A term of artisanship, as in ״חָרָשׁ חָכָם״ (Isaiah 40). And Onkelos interpreted, and changed in their interpretation, that a stone-craftsman is called אָמָן and a wood-craftsman is called נַגָּר." "<b>To set.</b> To set it in its setting in its setting-frame — to make the setting-frame to the measure of the seat of the stone and its thickness."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:56.602814193Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}